			<div class="content" id="post-content-1716853">
									

<p>Fly agaric is commonly used for it's psychotropic properites.<br />
I could imagine someone stumbling upon this little colony of what they think are &quot;magic mushrooms&quot; and harvesting them for fun and/or profit. It's pretty common for halluciongens to be consumed somewhere semi-private or at least away from the general public, to reduce risk of getting caught; there isn't a lot of direct sunlight in your average stoner basement/attic/living room/rave. The only unusual aspect for the first activation is the blood, and people &quot;under the influence&quot; are more prone to accidentally injuring themselves. Since the article isn't specific, it might only take a nasty papercut.</p>

