														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1733214">
									

<p>They do not need food in the traditional sense of the word. However,</p>
<blockquote>
<p>When a human being comes into direct skin contact with an instance of SCP-1627-A, all damage and infections present within them will be healed. Over the course of the following two (2) weeks, that subject will experience rapid senescence until death, often by natural causes associated with old age. This appears to give nourishment to the SCP-1627-A instance.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So, they don't need food and water ever, but if they go three or more weeks without touching someone, they die due to lack of nourishment. Comprendez-vous?</p>

							</div>

								
					
